---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Editable from '../components/content/Editable.astro';
import IdentityRichText from '../components/IdentityRichText.astro';
import { umjcMembershipValue } from '../data/congregationIdentity';
---
<PageLayout title="UMJC Membership - Kehilat Ohr HaTorah" pageTitle="Our UMJC Membership" description="Our place in the Union of Messianic Jewish Congregations: Torah covenant faithfulness, Jewish communal life, faith in Yeshua, and mutual support.">
    <div class="editorial-page">
        <section class="editorial-lead" aria-labelledby="umjc-lead-title">
            <div>
                <Editable field="umjc.lead-heading" as="h2" id="umjc-lead-title">Union of Messianic Jewish Congregations</Editable>
                <Editable field="umjc.lead-1" as="p"><strong>Kehilat Ohr HaTorah</strong> is a member of the Union of Messianic Jewish Congregations (UMJC).</Editable>
                <Editable field="umjc.lead-2" as="p">The UMJC brings congregations together around faith in Yeshua the Messiah and responsibility for Jewish covenant life. Its vision connects Torah, Jewish tradition, and the New Covenant with continuing participation in the life of the Jewish people.</Editable>
                <a class="text-link" href="https://www.umjc.org/vision" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><Editable field="umjc.link-vision">Read the UMJC’s vision</Editable> <i class="fas fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            </div>
            <aside class="editorial-side" aria-label="Our congregational identity">
                <ul class="editorial-link-list">
                    <li><a href="/mission#vision-and-purpose"><Editable field="umjc.side-vision-purpose">Vision and Purpose</Editable> <i class="fas fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a></li>
                    <li><a href="/mission#core-commitments"><Editable field="umjc.side-core-commitments">Core Commitments and Affirmations</Editable> <i class="fas fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a></li>
                    <li><a href="/mission#core-values"><Editable field="umjc.side-core-values">Core Values</Editable> <i class="fas fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a></li>
                </ul>
            </aside>
        </section>
        <section class="editorial-section editorial-split" aria-labelledby="membership-reason">
            <Editable field="umjc.membership-heading" as="h2" id="membership-reason">Why we belong</Editable>
            <div>
                <Editable field="umjc.membership-statement" as="p" class="membership-statement"><IdentityRichText content={umjcMembershipValue} /></Editable>
                <Editable field="umjc.membership-text" as="p">Membership connects our congregation with a wider community of learning, mutual support, and accountability. The union offers education and mentoring for congregational leaders, brings families together at conferences, and helps member communities support one another in times of need.</Editable>
                <a class="text-link" href="https://www.umjc.org/why-join-the-union" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><Editable field="umjc.link-union-serves">How the union serves its congregations</Editable> <i class="fas fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="editorial-section" aria-labelledby="shared-life">
            <Editable field="umjc.shared-life-heading" as="h2" id="shared-life">Jewish life in Messiah</Editable>
            <div class="editorial-columns">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="icon-heading"><i class="fas fa-scroll editorial-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><Editable field="umjc.torah-title">Torah and covenant faithfulness</Editable></h3>
                    <Editable field="umjc.torah-text" as="p">In the UMJC’s definition, Messianic Judaism shares the Jewish people’s history and covenantal responsibility. Scripture guides this life, while Jewish tradition connects present-day practice with earlier generations. Torah is lived and applied within the New Covenant.</Editable>
                    <a class="text-link" href="https://www.umjc.org/defining-messianic-judaism" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><Editable field="umjc.link-torah-definition">The UMJC’s definition of Messianic Judaism</Editable> <i class="fas fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="icon-heading"><i class="fas fa-people-group editorial-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><Editable field="umjc.unity-title">Unity and distinct callings</Editable></h3>
                    <Editable field="umjc.unity-text" as="p">The UMJC understands Jewish and non-Jewish followers of Yeshua as united in one Body of Messiah, with their distinct identities and callings preserved. Its vision values a full place within the Jewish people and a relationship of mutual blessing with the wider Christian community.</Editable>
                    <a class="text-link" href="/mission#core-commitments"><Editable field="umjc.link-unity-commitments">Read our congregation’s commitments</Editable> <i class="fas fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="editorial-section editorial-split">
            <Editable field="umjc.faith-heading" as="h2">Faith in Yeshua, Israel’s Messiah</Editable>
            <div>
                <Editable field="umjc.faith-1" as="p">The UMJC’s Statement of Faith affirms God’s enduring covenant with Israel, the authority of the Tanakh and New Covenant writings, and Yeshua’s atoning death and bodily resurrection. It looks forward to his return, the restoration of Israel, and the renewal of creation.</Editable>
                <Editable field="umjc.faith-2" as="p">These convictions belong within the Jewish communal life expressed in our congregation’s own Vision and Purpose, Core Commitments and Affirmations, and Core Values.</Editable>
                <a class="text-link" href="https://www.umjc.org/statement-of-faith" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><Editable field="umjc.link-statement-of-faith">Read the UMJC’s Statement of Faith</Editable> <i class="fas fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</PageLayout>
